//@version=6
// ==================================================================================================
//  XAUUSD SMART ENTRY ENGINE  -  Pine Script v6  -  INDICATOR ONLY
// ==================================================================================================
//
//  WHAT THIS IS
//  ------------
//  A complete market-map and high-confluence setup-detection engine, tuned for XAUUSD, built as a
//  pure INDICATOR (indicator()). It never uses strategy.* calls and never submits orders.
//  Every level it prints (entry / SL / TP1 / TP2 / TP3 / R:R / quality) is ANALYTICAL ONLY.
//
//  CORE LOGIC CHAIN
//  ----------------
//      HTF structure (H4 + H1)            -> environment / bias
//      Liquidity map (PD/PW/session/swing)-> where stops rest
//      Liquidity sweep (wick + close back)-> liquidity taken
//      Displacement (ATR + body + close)  -> intent
//      MSS / CHoCH (internal swing break) -> structure shift
//      Fair Value Gap                     -> entry zone
//      Retracement + confirmation         -> suggested entry
//      Logical liquidity targets          -> TP1 / TP2 / TP3
//      Risk / reward + confluence         -> setup quality score
//
//  NON-REPAINTING
//  --------------
//  * Every request.security() call uses barmerge.lookahead_off and barmerge.gaps_off.
//  * Higher-timeframe swings use ta.pivothigh / ta.pivotlow -> a pivot is only known AFTER
//    `length` bars have closed on that timeframe, so no future information is used.
//  * All state transitions (sweep -> displacement -> MSS -> FVG -> entry -> TP) only run on
//    CONFIRMED bars (barstate.isconfirmed). A developing sweep is shown as "POTENTIAL" until
//    the candle closes back through the level.
//  * Nothing is drawn, erased or re-coloured using data from a later bar.
//
//  IMPORTANT
//  ---------
//  "SETUP QUALITY: 85/100" is a CONFLUENCE SCORE, not a probability of profit.
//  Nothing here is a guarantee. Suggested entries are hypothetical / analytical only.
//
//  WHITESPACE / PASTING
//  --------------------
//  Pine blocks are INDENTATION BASED. This file uses 4 spaces per level - never tabs.
//  EVERY STATEMENT IS ON ONE LINE (nothing is ever wrapped), so the only indentation the
//  compiler has to read is block indentation - one level of 4 spaces per `if` / `for` /
//  `else` / function body. That removes Pine's "end of line without line continuation"
//  error class completely: a wrapped line must be indented MORE than the statement it
//  belongs to, and any paste path that flattens indentation breaks that rule.
//  If your paste path still eats leading spaces, the script will not compile (every `if` /
//  `for` body would sit at column 0). Two ways out:
//     1. paste from the RAW file (GitHub -> Raw / download), not from a rendered preview, or
//     2. use the tab-indented copy, XAUUSD_Smart_Entry_Engine.tabs.pine (same code, 1 tab
//        per level) - tabs survive paste paths that collapse runs of spaces.
//  TradingView also strips blank lines, so its line numbers will NOT match this file's.
//  To jump to a section, search for its header, e.g. "// 11 -" for the state machine.
//
//  CODE MAP
//  --------
//   1  INPUTS                    9   ORDER BLOCKS
//   2  USER-DEFINED TYPES        10  PREMIUM / DISCOUNT
//   3  HELPER FUNCTIONS          11  SETUP STATE MACHINE  (incl. entry / SL / TP engines,
//   4  CORE CALCULATIONS             quality score, invalidations, alerts)
//   5  HIGHER TIMEFRAME CONTEXT  12  RENDERING
//   6  SESSION ENGINE            13  CURRENT MARKET STATE + MARKET STORY
//   7  LIQUIDITY MAP +           14  DASHBOARD
//      SWEEP DETECTION           15  CURRENT STATE LABEL
//   8  FAIR VALUE GAP ENGINE
// ==================================================================================================

indicator(title = "XAUUSD Smart Entry Engine", shorttitle = "XAU-SMART-ENTRY", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

// ==================================================================================================
// 1 - INPUTS
// ==================================================================================================

